  "result": "I fixed it. `Cart.remove(sku)` in `shop/models.py:33` was checking each line's `item.name` (e.g. `'Widget'`) against the SKU you passed in, so `'sku-1'` never matched and no line was removed. It now checks `item.sku`, the same field `Cart.add` uses to find an existing line.\n\n- **Demo:** `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left) instead of `2`.\n- **Tests:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`, and all 6 pass. None of them covers `Cart.remove`, so if you want to stop this from coming back, the next step is to add a test for it.",
